# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
# No claims are used in more than one statement, so there are no claim lines.
# I found no bridge. P3 and P4 join different claims ("person" means an individual substance; the individual is distinct from others), and "individual" keeps one sense, as undivided in itself and distinct from others.
# S4 says "rational figure", but P3 reads it as "rational nature". This is a wording difference, not a shift between two senses within the argument.
